{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.yekutieli_leading_coefficient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.yekutieli_leading_coefficient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.yekutieli_obstruction_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.yekutieli_obstruction_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L271-L283","doc":"**Non-vanishing at `q ≠ 1`.**  Derived from the **sorry-free**\n`yekutieliObstructionData_kappaRaw_ne_zero` via the proved\n`obstructionCoord_eq_kappaRaw` (hence via `stokes_expansion`) — *not* via\nthe normalisation `raw_normalised`, so the non-vanishing rests on\ngenuinely proved content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.yekutieli_leading_coefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.yekutieli_leading_coefficient","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L251-L269","doc":"**Yekutieli obstruction = leading Chebyshev coefficient = 1**\n([`lem:yekutieli-leading-coefficient`]), at level `n = 5` for\n`T_{2,p}` with odd prime `p` and `q ≠ 1`.\n\n*Derived* (sorry-free): the proved `obstructionCoord_eq_kappaRaw` gives\n`κ = κ_raw`, `raw_normalised` gives `κ_raw = 1`, and\n`leadingChebyshev_eq_one` gives `c = 1`.  The theorem proves the\nidentity, it does not assume it.  This is the decl named by the content\nblock's `lean.ref`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:yekutieli-leading-coefficient","label":"lem:yekutieli-leading-coefficient","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/yekutieli-leading-coefficient.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.obstructionCoord_eq_kappaRaw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.obstructionCoord_eq_kappaRaw","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L240-L249","doc":"**`obstruction = κ_raw` — now PROVED, not axiomatised.**  The obstruction's\ngenus coordinate is the raw `d_q²` curvature, obtained from the polynomial\n`stokes_expansion` by the leading-coefficient extraction.  (Was the\naxiom `stokes_identity` in the earlier revision.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.obstructionCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.obstructionCoord","kind":"def","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L234-L238","doc":"The obstruction's **genus-filtration leading coordinate** — the leading\ncoefficient of its genus generating polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation.raw_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation.raw_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L232-L232","doc":"Normalisation: the raw curvature is unit-normalised (top coordinate\n`1`).  The irreducible normalisation input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation.stokes_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation.stokes_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L228-L228","doc":"**Non-abelian Stokes** (deep, not in Mathlib): the genus generating\npolynomial is the raw `d_q²` curvature times the monic genus-filtration\nChebyshev basis of degree `(p−1)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation.genusPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation.genusPoly","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L224-L224","doc":"The genus generating polynomial of the obstruction class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L221-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliStokesNormalisation","kind":"class","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L196-L232","doc":"**Yekutieli non-abelian Stokes normalisation (§3b-cond class).**\n\nThe genuinely deep, *not-in-Mathlib* input is now stated as a concrete\n**polynomial identity** rather than an opaque scalar equation:\n\n* `genusPoly` — the genus generating polynomial of the obstruction class\n  (its expansion in the genus filtration);\n* `stokes_expansion` — Yekutieli's non-abelian Stokes theorem says this\n  generating polynomial is the raw `d_q²` curvature times the monic\n  genus-filtration Chebyshev basis, `genusPoly = C κ_raw · monicCheb`.\n  A future formalisation of the `d_q²` curvature could *discharge* this\n  by computing `genusPoly` (`QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration`);\n* `raw_normalised` — the geometric data is unit-normalised so the top\n  genus coordinate is `1` (`κ_raw = 1`), the irreducible normalisation.\n\nProgress vs. the earlier revision: the scalar `stokes_identity`\n(`obstruction = κ_raw`) is **no longer an axiom** — it is the *derived*\n`obstructionCoord_eq_kappaRaw`, obtained from `stokes_expansion` by the\nproved leading-coefficient extraction `leadingCoeff_C_mul_monicCheb`.\nThe remaining axioms are the structural polynomial `stokes_expansion`\n(strictly stronger, but faithful to what non-abelian Stokes actually\nasserts) and the scalar `raw_normalised`.  `chebyshev_top_eq_one` stays\ndischarged (`leadingChebyshev_eq_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.leadingCoeff_C_mul_monicCheb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.leadingCoeff_C_mul_monicCheb","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L186-L194","doc":"**Genus-coordinate extraction (sorry-free).**  The leading coefficient of\n`scale · (monic basis)` is the scale itself — the genus-filtration\ncoordinate reads off the scale from a monic expansion.  This is the\nproved bridge that turns the polynomial Stokes expansion below into the\nscalar identity `obstruction = κ_raw`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.leadingChebyshev_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.leadingChebyshev_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L180-L184","doc":"**`c_{(p−1)/2} = 1`** — the genus-filtration basis is monic.  Discharges\nthe former `chebyshev_top_eq_one` axiom sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.leadingChebyshev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.leadingChebyshev","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L174-L178","doc":"The **leading Chebyshev coefficient** `c_{(p−1)/2}` of the\ngenus-filtration basis: the leading coefficient of the monic basis\npolynomial of degree `(p−1)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.monicCheb_monic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.monicCheb_monic","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L151-L172","doc":"`monicCheb S n` is monic of degree `n` (two-step induction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.monicCheb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.monicCheb","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L143-L149","doc":"**Monic Chebyshev-type basis**: `p₀ = 1`, `p₁ = X`,\n`p_{n+2} = X·p_{n+1} − p_n`.  Monic of degree `n` by construction — the\nsubtracted lower-degree term never reaches the top coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.yekutieliObstructionData_kappaRaw_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.yekutieliObstructionData_kappaRaw_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L114-L130","doc":"**Raw obstruction non-vanishing (sorry-free).**\n\nFor `q ≠ 1`, the `d_q²` curvature value `κ_raw` is nonzero — the actual\nreason `κ(T_{2,p}) ≠ 0` away from the classical limit `q = 1`: the\nuniversal `d_q²` coefficient `q⁻¹(1 − q⁻¹)` vanishes iff `q = 1`, and the\ngeometric factors `w`, `ν` are nonzero by nondegeneracy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.kappaRaw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.kappaRaw","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L106-L112","doc":"The **raw curvature value** of the Yekutieli obstruction,\n`κ_raw = q⁻¹(1 − q⁻¹) · w · ν` — the `d_q²` formula of the narrative\nproof (`prop:categorical-dq-squared`).  A `def` of the data (not a\nfree field) so that `..._kappaRaw_ne_zero` is non-vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.wedge_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.wedge_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The `q`-wedge of the two independent `1`-forms is nondegenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.wedge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.wedge","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The `q`-wedge value `ν = ω_V ∧_q ω_T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.weight_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.weight_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L98-L98","doc":"The weight of a genuine top cycle is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.weight","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The `T`-action weight `w` of the top Seifert cycle `γ₅` (the `5`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.q","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The substrate parameter `q`, carried as a **unit** of the ground\nring: algebraic invertibility (the old `q ≠ 0`), not the\narchimedean `0 < q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.YekutieliObstructionData","kind":"structure","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/yekutieli_leading_coefficient.lean#L82-L102","doc":"**Geometric data of the level-`n` Yekutieli obstruction for `T_{2,p}`.**\n\nThe substrate `q` (with algebraic invertibility witness), the `T`-action\n`weight` `w` of the top Seifert cycle `γ₅` (the integer `5`, nonzero),\nand the `q`-wedge value `wedge` `ν = ω_V ∧_q ω_T` (nondegenerate,\nnonzero).  The nonzero witnesses are geometric-nondegeneracy inputs,\ncarried as data so the non-vanishing theorem below is non-vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0}]}